byte-for-byte, since those target a different rendering surface (a
terminal color quantizer).

================================================================================
2. Tokyo Night — accent colors
================================================================================

The blue/purple/green/orange accent hues layered on top of the neutral
grayscale (used for syntax highlighting, links, and selection) trace back to
the original Tokyo Night VS Code theme. This is the primary/original source
for these accents — its rule names (e.g. the "Italics - Comments, Storage,
Keyword Flow, Vue attributes, Decorators" TextMate scope grouping) appear
verbatim in Grok Build's tmTheme assets, confirming that lineage.

